-## 5. Video Proof & Query Endpoints (Admin & CSKH)
+## 4. Video Query & Remote Range Streaming
 
-### 5.1. `GET /api/v1/videos`
-Search video records by metadata.
+### 4.1. `GET /api/v1/videos/:id/stream`
+Streams video content with HTTP 206 Partial Content byte-range support.
 
-**Query Parameters:**
-- `trackingCode` (string)
-- `orderCode` (string)
-- `startDate` (ISO string)
-- `endDate` (ISO string)
-- `stationId` (UUID)
-- `userId` (UUID)
-- `warehouseId` (UUID)
-- `disputeStatus` (NORMAL | DISPUTE | RESOLVED)
-- `page` (number, default: 1)
-- `limit` (number, default: 20)
+**Headers Supported:**
+```http
+Range: bytes=0-1048575
+```
 
-### 5.2. `GET /api/v1/videos/:id/stream`
-Streams the video with full HTTP 206 Partial Content byte-range support for seamless seeking.
+**Location Resolution:**
+1. If `videos.sync_status === 'SYNCED'`: Backend API reads file from NAS path `\\SERVER\PackingVideo\...`.
+2. If `videos.sync_status !== 'SYNCED'` (file remains on Station PC): Backend API transparently reverse-proxies the stream request to the station worker's internal stream endpoint (`http://<station-ip>:4005/worker/video/:id/stream`), authenticated with a short-lived HMAC token.
 
-### 5.3. `POST /api/v1/videos/:id/verify-hash`
-Re-computes file hash on demand and compares it with the immutable database record.
